⟨{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{1}^{9}1\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{t}\\,\\,{|}_{1}^{9},\\,t\\,\\,{|}_{1}^{9}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{9}-\\sqrt{1},\\,9-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-99361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04eca659e09dc9a77301cd7af598024ca582eee954e6337d97e460da43fbcc92"} {"question" "q-99361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-99361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨2,\\,8⟩"] ["math" "⟨8,\\,8⟩"] ["math" "⟨9,\\,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{3},\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{6},\\,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-99361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2,\\,8⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨20{t}^{3},\\,16t({t}^{2}-1)⟩$ and $F(1)=⟨1,\\,5⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨20{t}^{3},\\,16t({t}^{2}-1)⟩\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨20{t}^{3},\\,16t({t}^{2}-1)⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 20{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 16t({t}^{2}-1)\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5{t}^{4}+{c}_{1},\\,4{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨1,\\,5⟩$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨5\\cdot {1}^{4}+{c}_{1},\\,4{({1}^{2}-1)}^{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,5⟩ \\\\ ⟨5+{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=-4$ and ${c}_{2}=5.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨5{t}^{4}-4,\\,4{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+5⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04eca659e09dc9a77301cd7af598024ca582eee954e6337d97e460da43fbcc92"} {"question" "q-123473" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123473" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨5{t}^{3}-5,\\,4{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+4⟩"] ["math" "⟨5{t}^{4}+4,\\,4{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+5⟩"] ["math" "⟨5{t}^{4}-4,\\,4{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+5⟩"] ["math" "⟨5{t}^{5}-4,\\,4{(t-1)}^{2}+5⟩"] ["math" "⟨{t}^{2}-4,\\,4{({t}^{4}-1)}^{2}-5⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123473" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨5{t}^{4}-4,\\,4{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+5⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\frac{16\\sqrt[3]{t}}{3},\\,5{e}^{5t}⟩$ and $F(0)=⟨2,\\,-1⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\frac{16\\sqrt[3]{t}}{3},\\,5{e}^{5t}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\frac{16\\sqrt[3]{t}}{3},\\,5{e}^{5t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\frac{16\\sqrt[3]{t}}{3}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 5{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{4/3}+{c}_{1},\\,{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(0)=⟨2,\\,-1⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)=⟨4\\cdot {0}^{4/3}+{c}_{1},\\,{e}^{5\\cdot 0}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ ⟨{c}_{1},\\,1+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=2$ and ${c}_{2}=-2.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨4{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,{e}^{5t}-2⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04eca659e09dc9a77301cd7af598024ca582eee954e6337d97e460da43fbcc92"} {"question" "q-123474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨4{t}^{1/3}+1,\\,{e}^{t}-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨4{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,5{e}^{5t}-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨4{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,{e}^{5t}-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨4{t}^{4/3}-2,\\,{e}^{5t}-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,{e}^{2t}-5⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,{e}^{5t}-2⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\,,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩$ and $F(\\pi )=⟨-3,\\,3⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\,,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\,,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(\\pi )=⟨-3,\\,3⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\pi )=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi )+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨-3,\\,3⟩ \\\\ ⟨-1+{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨-3,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=-2$ and ${c}_{2}=3.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+3⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04eca659e09dc9a77301cd7af598024ca582eee954e6337d97e460da43fbcc92"} {"question" "q-123472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+3⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+3⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+3⟩"] ["math" "⟨{sec}^{2}⁡t-3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+3⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t⟩$ and $F(1)=⟨1,\\,3⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\frac{2}{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 2t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|+{c}_{1},\\,{t}^{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})+{c}_{1},\\,{t}^{2}+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨1,\\,3⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{2})+{c}_{1},\\,(1)^{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,3⟩ \\\\ ⟨{c}_{1},\\,1+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=2.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})+1,\\,{t}^{2}+2⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04eca659e09dc9a77301cd7af598024ca582eee954e6337d97e460da43fbcc92"} {"question" "q-123470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})+1,\\,{t}^{2}+2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})+1,\\,{t}^{2}-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})-1,\\,{t}^{2}+1⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})-2,\\,t+2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,{t}^{2}+2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-123470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})+1,\\,{t}^{2}+2⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-85742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,,{sec}^{2}⁡(t)⟩$ and $F(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=⟨1,\\,0⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-85742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,,{sec}^{2}⁡(t)⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,,{sec}^{2}⁡(t)⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=⟨1,\\,0⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨\\frac{1}{2}+{c}_{1},\\,1+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-1.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)-1⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-85742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04eca659e09dc9a77301cd7af598024ca582eee954e6337d97e460da43fbcc92"} {"question" "q-85742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-85742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\frac{1}{2},\\,2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(t)+2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+1,\\,2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(t)-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-1,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)-1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "q-85742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)-1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3966a8fb4d6c3ed445f7fd047396bd6ce60b6042d11d31c1d3ab32a30163a24"} {"question" "e-612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\mathbf F(t)$ given that $\\mathbf F'(t)= \\langle 6t^5+2t, \\sec^2 t\\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/example-612.json" "file_sha256" "756a84fac8544de6073a5e0a69586616380f4c7c2b860b805325d67032294e30"} {"question" "e-612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle 6t^5+2t,\\, \\sec^2 t\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨6{t}^{5}+2t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int (6{t}^{5}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int {sec}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2}+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/example-612.json" "file_sha256" "756a84fac8544de6073a5e0a69586616380f4c7c2b860b805325d67032294e30"} {"question" "e-613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\left\\langle\\cos(2t+1), \\, 4\\right\\rangle \\,\\textrm d t\\,.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/example-613.json" "file_sha256" "f7b9c97f25f78fb43d2267d607cb9a71c12fcfe325eccdf5b3b7502549eca41e"} {"question" "e-613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1),\\,4⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 4\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t) =\\cos(2t+1),$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u= 2t +1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d t} = 2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d t = \\dfrac 1 2 \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)+{c}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1)+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) =4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int 4\\text{d}t=4t+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1),\\,4⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1)+{c}_{1},\\,4t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1),\\,4t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1),\\,4t⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/example-613.json" "file_sha256" "f7b9c97f25f78fb43d2267d607cb9a71c12fcfe325eccdf5b3b7502549eca41e"} {"question" "e-614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{2} \\left\\langle 2e^{t},\\, 6t^2\\right\\rangle\\, \\textrm d t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/example-614.json" "file_sha256" "96f51f7f38fe88727c905081baabaadc2f9034c6afa8e8e61fb39805f381196d"} {"question" "e-614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨2{e}^{t},\\,6{t}^{2}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t⟩. \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{t}\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨[2{e}^{2}-2{e}^{0}],\\,[2\\cdot {2}^{3}-0]⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2}-2,\\,16⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/example-614.json" "file_sha256" "96f51f7f38fe88727c905081baabaadc2f9034c6afa8e8e61fb39805f381196d"} {"question" "e-615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\mathbf F(t)$ given that $\\mathbf F'(t)= \\left\\langle \\sec t \\tan t, \\,  \\sin(2t)\\right\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf F(0)=\\langle 0,\\, 0\\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/example-615.json" "file_sha256" "d20b293111cbac091c31683dcc52114e4ea9fb8f1336f3e8df1883ee0a406644"} {"question" "e-615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle \\sec t \\tan t,\\,  \\sin(2t)\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $\\mathbf F(0)=\\left\\langle 0,\\, 0 \\right\\rangle$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡0+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨1+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨0,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $c_1=-1$ and $c_2=\\dfrac 12.$ Consequently, \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\left\\langle  \\sec t - 1  , \\,  -\\dfrac 1 2\\cos(2t)+ \\dfrac12\\right\\rangle.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/example-615.json" "file_sha256" "d20b293111cbac091c31683dcc52114e4ea9fb8f1336f3e8df1883ee0a406644"}] "usage" {"e-612" [] "q-50201" [] "e-614" [] "e-613" [] "e-615" [] "q-99361" [] "q-123224" []} "basis" 1820 "retractions" [[17592186097224 :question/problem "Find $∫⟨\\frac{3}{t}, \\frac{5}{t^{2}}⟩dt$."] [17592186097318 :question/problem "What is $∫_{1}^{9}⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}, 1⟩dt$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186095702 17592186095703 17592186095704 17592186095705 17592186095706 17592186096266 17592186096267 17592186096268 17592186096269 17592186096270 17592186297271 17592186297272 17592186297273 17592186297274 17592186297275] "immutable_fields" [[17592186095701 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095701 :answer-field/id] [17592186095701 :answer-field/key] [17592186095701 :answer-field/type] [17592186096265 :answer-field/correct] [17592186096265 :answer-field/id] [17592186096265 :answer-field/key] [17592186096265 :answer-field/type] [17592186297270 :answer-field/correct] [17592186297270 :answer-field/id] [17592186297270 :answer-field/key] [17592186297270 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
